# UI border radius

Use **two consistent radii** when designing or implementing UI. Do not mix other sizes (`rounded-md`, `rounded-2xl`, arbitrary `rounded-[…]`) unless the user asks for an exception.

## `rounded-xl` — containers and overlays

- **Cards** — content cards, list items styled as cards, empty-state panels
- **Modals** — dialog panels, drawers styled as modal surfaces
- **Popovers** — dropdown menus, floating panels, tooltips with a boxed surface

Nested content flush with the card edge may use `rounded-none`; the **outer** shell still uses `rounded-xl`.

## `rounded-lg` — everything else

- **Buttons** — all variants (primary, secondary, outline, ghost); icon-only pills may use `rounded-full`
- **Inputs** — text, email, password, search, textarea
- **Selects** — native `<select>`, custom select triggers (menus/popover panels use `rounded-xl`)
- **Other controls** — chips, alerts, toggle groups, filter pills, combobox triggers

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<button className="rounded-lg bg-primary px-4 py-2 text-white">Save</button>
<input className="rounded-lg border border-secondary/30 bg-surface px-3 py-2" />
<article className="rounded-xl border border-secondary/15 bg-surface p-4">…</article>
<div className="rounded-xl bg-surface p-6 shadow-lg" role="dialog">…</div>
<div className="rounded-xl border bg-surface py-1 shadow-md">…popover…</div>

// ❌ BAD
<button className="rounded-xl …">  {/* buttons use rounded-lg */}
<article className="rounded-lg …">  {/* cards use rounded-xl */}
```

## Shared UI folder

Encode radii in `src/components/ui/` base styles: **`rounded-lg`** in button, select trigger, input; **`rounded-xl`** in card (and modal/popover when added).
